    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0359" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg347"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79690/47: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Farrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-25T18:00:00+03:00">June 25, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>128. Department’s 95, May 19;<anchor n="10" xml:id="d407-f1"/> and Legation’s 126
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">127</hi>], July [<hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>]
                    22. Basra customs authorities demanding cash payment of duty on Pan American
                    imports for improving Basra airport despite local guarantees of payment of [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">as?</hi>] Pan American does not <pb facs="0360" n="348"
                        xml:id="pg348"/> acquire customs exemption as an agency of the United States
                    Government. Legation will appreciate indication of present status of
                    negotiations regarding Pan American in Iraq.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department repeated to Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Farrell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
